UPDATE companies SET description='Aftermarket HQ operates from Las Vegas, Nevada, where it has served the off-road community for over a decade. The shop was established by enthusiasts who wanted a destination that combined parts retail with hands-on fabrication and tuning, though the exact founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed. The team includes Walt, Evan, Vanessa, and Jamie, who are referenced in customer testimonials as the faces behind the counter and the builds.

The business stocks and installs performance components for late-model trucks and SUVs — primarily Ford F-150, Raptor, Bronco, and Ranger platforms. Its catalog covers LED lighting from Baja Designs, stainless-steel downpipes from SPD, third-party brake-light assemblies with integrated Starlink mounts from SwarfWorks, switch-panel power systems, and wiring harnesses. In-house services span suspension upgrades, custom fabrication, complete vehicle builds, ECU flashing, and powder-coating in a matte fine-textured black finish.

Customers are recreational and competitive off-roaders who run desert dunes, rock trails, and daily-driven rigs. Buyers range from first-time modifiers to owners of six-figure custom builds who return for follow-up tuning and service.

The company positions its edge on lived experience — every product sold has been tested on the terrain it''s meant for, and every build is tuned on-site. That "built by enthusiasts, for enthusiasts" ethos, coupled with 10-plus years of continuous operation in the Las Vegas Valley, is cited as the reason customers trust the shop with high-value vehicles.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom fabrication", "Suspension system installation and tuning", "Complete off-road vehicle builds", "LED lighting installation (Baja Designs)", "Stainless steel exhaust/downpipe installation (SPD)", "Third-party brake light assembly installation with Starlink mount (SwarfWorks)", "Switch panel power system installation (SP9100)", "Wiring harness installation", "ECU tuning and flashing", "Starlink mount installation", "Powder coating (matte fine-textured black outdoor)", "Replaceable lens/optics service (uService)"], "industries": ["Off-road automotive aftermarket", "Truck and SUV performance customization", "Automotive performance parts retail and installation"], "materials": ["304 Stainless Steel", "16-gauge steel", "CNC billet aluminum", "Powder coating media (matte fine-textured black)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Tested in the desert \u2014 every product validated on actual off-road terrain", "10+ years of continuous operation as a Las Vegas off-road performance shop", "Custom fabrication and complete vehicle builds performed in-house", "ECU tuning and flashing capability for Ford platforms", "Matte fine-textured outdoor powder-coating offered as a finish option"], "facts_used": ["Location: Las Vegas, Nevada -> db", "Business type: off-road performance shop selling parts and providing installation/custom fabrication -> website homepage", "Experience: 10+ years / over a decade in Las Vegas Valley -> website homepage", "Team members: Walt, Evan, Vanessa, Jamie mentioned in testimonials -> website homepage", "Brands carried: Baja Designs, SwarfWorks, SPD -> website homepage product listings", "Services: suspension systems, custom fabrication, complete off-road builds, tuning, powder coating -> website homepage", "Customer base: off-road enthusiasts, Ford F150/Raptor/Bronco/Ranger owners -> website homepage and product listings", "Differentiators: tested in desert, built by enthusiasts for enthusiasts -> website homepage", "Materials: 304SS downpipes, 16ga steel brackets, CNC billet aluminum mounts -> website homepage product descriptions"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "For 10+ years, Aftermarket HQ has been Vegas''s go-to shop for real off-road performance upgrades. Whether it''s suspension systems, custom fabrication, or complete off-road builds, our work speaks for itself", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='aftermarket-hq' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Agave Semiconductor operates from Phoenix, Arizona, where it develops semiconductor solutions for electric motor control. The company was founded as a startup within the Arizona technology community, though its founding year and ownership structure have not been publicly disclosed. Its founder has discussed the local startup ecosystem in regional business media.

The company designs and supplies pre-driver integrated circuits for brushless DC fan controllers, offered in both open-loop (AGV8011, AGV8012, AGV8018, AGV8019) and closed-loop (AGV8001, AGV8002, AGV8008, AGV8009) configurations. Its core Smart-Drive technology adjusts power delivery to fan motors in real time, optimizing energy efficiency while maintaining mechanical workload. The AGV8009 closed-loop pre-driver includes features such as precise RPM feedback, soft start, current limiting, locked-rotor protection, and thermal shutdown, with 40 V MOS outputs capable of sourcing or sinking 100 mA.

Agave’s products target data center operators and equipment manufacturers that rely on fans and blowers for thermal management. By optimizing the pressure-airflow operating point, the technology aims to reduce the electricity consumed by cooling systems while preserving required airflow.

Agave states that its Smart-Drive approach can achieve energy savings of up to 80 percent depending on fan pressure and airflow conditions, and that it reduces motor vibration as a secondary benefit. The company describes its mission as improving electric motor efficiency and performance through intelligent control.', certifications=ARRAY['RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Semiconductor design", "IC design for brushless DC motor control", "Open-loop pre-driver development", "Closed-loop pre-driver development", "Real-time efficiency optimization algorithms", "Motor control firmware development", "Fan controller IC design"], "industries": ["Data centers"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Real-time motor efficiency optimization via Smart-Drive technology", "Up to 80% energy savings in fan applications", "Reduced motor vibration", "Closed-loop RPM control with integrated protections (current limit, locked rotor, thermal)", "40 V MOS pre-driver outputs with 100 mA source/sink capability"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "Product lines: AGV8000 series open-loop and closed-loop pre-drivers -> page /", "Smart-Drive technology for real-time motor efficiency optimization -> page /", "Data center cooling fan applications -> page /", "RoHS certification -> db", "Company mission: improving electric motor efficiency through intelligent control -> page /", "AGV8009 features: closed-loop feedback, soft start, protections, 40V MOS outputs -> page /", "Founder mentioned in Arizona startup community context -> page /", "Contact address: 3930 E Ray Road, Suite 140, Phoenix, AZ 85044 -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "AGV8009 Closed Loop Pre-Driver The AGV8009 provides all the features required for 3 or 4 wire fan control.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='agave-semiconductor' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Agri-Industrial Plastics Co. was founded in 1978 by Dick Smith in Fairfield, Iowa. The company began by collaborating with trade leaders to advance plastic blow molding technology and later invested in equipment to produce EPA-compliant fuel tanks.

The company operates a 340,000-square-foot manufacturing facility in Fairfield housing 20 monolayer accumulator-head blow molding machines and eight multilayer continuous coextrusion machines dedicated to non-automotive fuel tank production. Its core processes include custom and extrusion blow molding, supported by engineering and design services, quality control, assembly, and packaging. The plant focuses on large-scale industrial parts such as fuel tanks and components for turf equipment, powersports, agricultural, and marine applications.

Agri-Industrial serves customers in the turf equipment, power sports, agricultural, marine, recreational equipment, lawn and garden, and watercraft industries. Notable clients referenced include EXCEL Industries/Hustler Turf Equipment, Kubota Manufacturing of America, and John Deere, all of which rely on the company for critical blow-molded components.

The company''s stated vision is to be the provider of innovative, high-quality blow molded solutions. Its quality management system is certified to ISO 9001:2015 (without design) and includes APQP, Level III PPAP capability, hourly production inspections, and a Shape Grabber laser scanner for 3D dimensional verification against CAD models.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Blow Molding", "Extrusion Blow Molding", "Engineering & Design Support", "Quality Control", "Manufacturing", "Assembly & Packaging", "On-Time Delivery", "Part and Mold Design", "APQP (Advanced Production Quality Planning)", "Level III PPAP", "Laser Scanning Inspection (Shape Grabber)", "EPA-Compliant Fuel Tank Production"], "industries": ["Turf Equipment", "Power Sports", "Agricultural", "Marine", "Recreational Equipment", "Lawn & Garden", "Water Craft"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["20 monolayer accumulator-head industrial blow molding machines", "8 multilayer continuous coextrusion machines", "Shape Grabber Laser Scanner"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["340,000 sq ft facility with 20 monolayer and 8 multilayer coextrusion blow molding machines", "ISO 9001:2015 certified (without design) by Smithers Quality Assessments", "Level III PPAP capability and APQP implementation", "Shape Grabber laser scanner for 3D part-to-CAD comparison", "Specialization in EPA-compliant non-automotive fuel tanks"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1978 by Dick Smith in Fairfield, Iowa -> /about-us", "Family succession: daughter Lori became president in 2015 -> db", "340,000 sq ft facility with 20 monolayer and 8 multilayer coex machines -> /about-us", "ISO 9001:2015 certified (without design) by Smithers -> /quality", "Level III PPAP capability and APQP -> /quality", "Shape Grabber laser scanner for 3D inspection -> /quality", "Industries: turf equipment, power sports, agricultural, marine, recreational, lawn & garden, watercraft -> /about-us, /quality", "Customers: EXCEL Industries/Hustler Turf, Kubota Manufacturing, John Deere -> /", "Vision: leading provider of innovative, high-quality blow molded solutions -> /about-us", "Core processes: custom blow molding, extrusion blow molding, engineering & design, quality control, assembly & packaging -> /, /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Agri-Industrial Plastics is a certified custom industrial blow molder of large scale parts.", "founded_year": "1978", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='agri-industrial-plastics-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Air Metal was founded in 1970 by Douglas and Gladys Smith in Richmond, Virginia. Since 2021, the company has continued the legacy established by the Smiths, operating a fabrication shop with over 60 years of combined fabrication experience.

The company operates a full-service fabrication shop producing a wide range of sheet metal products. Core offerings include standing seam roofing panels in snap lock (1" or 1.5"), mechanical lock (1", 1.5", or 2"), and nail strip (1" or 1.5") profiles, as well as 5V Crimp panels and commercial 2" mechanical lock systems. The shop also fabricates metal soffit and wall panels, fascia, valleys, coping, drip edge, and custom accessories such as chimney caps, cupolas, conductor heads, and vents. Historic duplication of metalwork is a noted specialty. In addition, Air Metal manufactures HVAC components including ducting and fittings, plenums, diffuser boxes, and register boxes.

The company emphasizes its ability to handle projects of any size, supported by its in-house fabrication capabilities.

The company distinguishes itself through its deep fabrication experience and focus on weather-resistant roofing systems suited to Virginia''s climate. The Smiths'' original commitment to quality remains a guiding principle, and the current team highlights the shop''s combined six decades of hands-on expertise as a key differentiator for customers seeking custom metal solutions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom sheet metal fabrication", "Standing seam roofing panel fabrication (Snaplock, Mechanical Lock, Nail Strip)", "5V Crimp metal roofing panel fabrication", "Metal soffit and wall panel fabrication", "Fascia panel fabrication", "Valley fabrication", "Coping fabrication", "Drip edge fabrication", "Historic metalwork duplication", "Custom gutter fabrication", "Chimney cap fabrication", "Cupola fabrication", "Conductor head fabrication", "Vent fabrication", "Ducting and fitting fabrication", "Plenum fabrication", "Diffuser box fabrication", "Register box fabrication"], "industries": ["Construction", "Roofing", "HVAC"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 60 years of combined fabrication experience in-house", "Specializes in Snaplock, 5V Crimp, and nailstrip standing seam roofing panels", "Offers historic duplication of architectural metalwork", "Full-service fabrication shop handling projects of any size", "Custom gutter, soffit, and roofing accessory fabrication"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1970 by Douglas and Gladys Smith -> /about", "Located in Richmond, Virginia -> db", "Custom sheet metal fabrication and metal roofing -> /", "Specializes in Snaplock, 5V Crimp, nailstrip standing seam panels -> /", "Fabricates gutters, soffits, chimney caps, cupolas, conductor heads, vents -> /", "Provides ducting, fittings, plenums, diffuser boxes, register boxes -> /", "Over 60 years combined fabrication experience -> /about", "Serves Central Virginia region -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Your full service sheet metal fabricator, and metal roofing experts in Richmond, Virginia.", "founded_year": "1970", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='air-metal-va' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Link Labs, based in Annapolis, Maryland, was founded in 2014 by a group of veteran engineers from the Johns Hopkins University Applied Physics Laboratory. The team had previously collaborated on projects for the U.S. Department of Defense, the telecommunications industry, and the intelligence community.

The company develops the AirFinder platform, an end-to-end IoT asset visibility system that combines hardware and software to track assets indoors and outdoors. Its product line includes BLE and Xtreme Low Energy (XLE®) tags, location beacons, access points, and gateways, all managed through a cloud-based interface. Link Labs reports processing more than two billion location, condition, and behavior events per month and holds 29 U.S. patents with additional international patents.

AirFinder serves manufacturing, logistics, election administration, and healthcare sectors. In manufacturing and logistics, customers use the system for work-in-process tracking, inventory management, tool and equipment monitoring, and trailer tracking. Election officials deploy it to track voting equipment and personnel, while hospitals use it to locate medical devices and monitor environmental conditions for compliance.

Link Labs says its differentiation rests on four pillars: combining multiple location technologies to provide the right accuracy at the lowest total cost; supporting a wide range of tags and sensors for diverse use cases; offering enterprise-grade scalability with global 5G connectivity and API/MQTT integration; and delivering a market-validated solution backed by billions of monthly events and a patented technology base.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["IoT asset tracking and monitoring", "Real-time location services (RTLS)", "Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) asset tracking", "Xtreme Low Energy (XLE\u00ae) technology", "Phase ranging location", "Indoor and outdoor asset tracking", "Environmental monitoring (temperature, humidity, shock, tampering)", "Geofencing and alerting", "Dwell time monitoring", "Route and transit monitoring", "Cloud-based asset visibility platform", "MQTT and API integration", "Global 5G connectivity", "Asset tag hardware design and manufacturing", "Beacon and gateway hardware design and manufacturing", "Software platform development"], "industries": ["Manufacturing", "Logistics", "Elections", "Healthcare"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Annapolis, Maryland -> /about", "Founded: 2014 -> /about", "Founders: veteran engineers from Johns Hopkins APL -> /about", "Product: AirFinder platform (hardware tags, beacons, gateways, software) -> /, /services", "Technologies: BLE, XLE, phase ranging, GPS, Wi-Fi, cellular -> /, /services", "Accuracy: up to 30 cm -> /", "Scale: 2+ billion events/month, 29 US patents -> /", "Industries: Manufacturing, Logistics, Elections, Healthcare -> /, /services", "Differentiators: multiple location tech, use case extensibility, lowest total cost, enterprise scalability -> /", "Hardware components: Location Beacon, Asset Tag, AirFinder Access Point, Gateway -> /", "Environmental sensors: temperature, humidity, shock, tampering -> /", "Geofencing, dwell time, route monitoring -> /", "MQTT/API integration, global 5G -> /", "Battery life up to 7 years -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "AirFinder OnSite is the first Bluetooth-based RTLS that provides up to meter-level indoor accuracy. This system uses Bluetooth Low Energy (LE) and phase ranging for reduced latency within a specified geo-fence. AirFinder OnSite''s flexible architecture tracks items within a warehouse or facility with an up to 7-year battery life and enhanced power to track work-in-process (WIP), inventory, equipment, tools, packages, personnel, and beyond.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='airfinder' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Aire Plastics is a family-owned injection molding company based in La Vernia, Texas, founded in 1989. The business traces its roots to 1982 when mold maker Ken Simms established Aire Masters of San Antonio after moving from Colorado. Following Simms'' unexpected death in 1989, Terry Post, who owned an automotive repair business on family property in Adkins, Texas, acquired the plastics division and converted his garage into a production plant. Despite lacking prior molding experience, Post applied his background in high-precision boiler fabrication to deliver on-time parts to the company''s original six customers.

Today the company operates a highly automated facility housing nine injection molding machines with press capacities ranging from 33 to 275 tons. The shop offers insert molding, over-molding, rapid tooling, prototyping, 3D modeling, and proof-of-concept development, along with secondary services such as ultrasonic welding, clam-shell packaging, packaging design, and direct-to-distribution shipping. A staff of 14 handles production runs from low-volume prototypes to high-volume orders.

Aire Plastics serves a mix of long-standing clients — including the original six accounts from 1989 — as well as inventors, entrepreneurs, and product developers seeking manufacturing support. The company emphasizes intellectual property protection, requiring non-disclosure agreements before project discussions, and provides resources for product development stages from ideation through manufacturing.

