UPDATE companies SET description='Albuquerque Apparel Center operates in Albuquerque, New Mexico, as a physical and online hub for the state''s apparel and accessory industry. The center was established to connect designers, suppliers, production houses, merchants, and visitors with resources, supplies, employment, and industry-related services.

The center provides a range of services including a networking hub with multi-media promotional advertising and events such as fashion shows and seminars, a retail outlet where designers can sell directly to customers while connecting with wholesale buyers, and an online destination site, NMFashionInfo.com, listing apparel stores, supplies, services, and events across New Mexico. It also runs the AAC School of Fashion Design, offering classes in flat pattern design, draping, sewing, and couture garment construction for all ages, along with mentorship programs for schools and organizations. Custom design and pattern services are available for start-ups and established businesses.

The center serves the broader fashion and apparel industry in New Mexico, targeting independent designers, apparel start-ups, production houses, retail merchants, and educational institutions. It also works with community organizations such as battered women''s groups and rehabilitation facilities, providing fashion design classes as a pathway to employment and self-sufficiency.

The center''s stated mission is to foster the growth of New Mexico''s apparel industry by leveraging the state''s unique Southwest, Native American, and Western styles, lower cost of living, and local creative talent. It positions itself as a support system that guides businesses from concept to consumer, aiming to create jobs and retain the economic benefits of New Mexico''s distinctive fashion heritage within the state.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Networking and industry promotion", "Retail sales outlet for designers", "Online industry directory (NMFashionInfo.com)", "Business guidance for apparel start-ups", "Custom design and pattern services", "Fashion design classes and workshops", "Mentorship programs for schools and organizations", "Community fashion design training for underserved groups"], "industries": ["Apparel and accessory industry", "Fashion design education", "Textile and clothing manufacturing support"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Physical and online hub connecting the entire state to resources, supplies, and employment", "Retail outlet allowing designers to sell directly to customers while accessing wholesale buyers", "NMFashionInfo.com online destination for all New Mexico apparel stores, supplies, and events", "AAC School of Fashion Design offering classes in pattern design, draping, sewing, and couture construction", "Fashion design classes for battered women''s groups and rehabilitation facilities as a ''hand up'' program"], "facts_used": ["Location: Albuquerque, New Mexico -> db", "Operates as physical and online hub for NM apparel industry -> /about", "Provides networking hub with promotional advertising, fashion shows, seminars -> /about", "Offers retail outlet for designers to sell direct and connect with wholesale buyers -> /about", "Runs NMFashionInfo.com online directory of NM apparel stores, supplies, services, events -> /about", "Ope