UPDATE companies SET description='Alcan Electric & Engineering was founded in 1971 in Anchorage, Alaska, and remains Alaskan-owned and operated. The company has grown from a traditional electrical contractor into a full-service technology integrator with offices in Anchorage, Fairbanks, Juneau, and Wasilla, serving the entire state from the Arctic to the Gulf Coast.

The firm employs more than 200 professionals and provides commercial electrical construction — power distribution, lighting, backup power, high-voltage systems, and design engineering — alongside low-voltage technology integration: security and access control (including IP video surveillance as Alaska’s Milestone pioneer), communications and VoIP, structured cabling (BICSI-certified copper and fiber, and the state’s only Corning preferred installer), audio-visual systems, commercial solar, EV charging infrastructure, and NFPA 70B-aligned electrical maintenance programs.

Alcan serves healthcare, aviation, corrections, defense, North Slope industry, and commercial clients. Notable projects include a 15-year partnership with Providence Alaska Medical Center encompassing the 82,000-square-foot Tower M, electrical work for the 16-bay F-35 hangars at Eielson Air Force Base, and advanced smartphone-controlled systems at the Anchorage Fish Hatchery.

The company emphasizes its Alaskan roots as a differentiator: 50-plus years of experience with the state’s conditions, codes, and logistics; a workforce trained through NECA and IBEW Local 1547; a formal safety program called Safety Zone; and the convenience of a single integrated partner for both electrical and low-voltage technology systems.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Commercial electrical construction", "Power distribution", "Lighting design and installation", "Backup power systems", "High-voltage systems", "Electrical design & engineering", "Electrical system integration", "Building automation", "Security & access control", "IP video surveillance", "Communications & VoIP", "Unified communications", "Structured cabling (copper & fiber)", "BICSI-certified installation", "Audio visual systems", "Commercial solar installation", "EV charging station installation", "NFPA 70B electrical maintenance"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Aviation", "Corrections", "Defense", "North Slope industry", "Industrial", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Alaska-only Corning preferred installer for structured cabling", "Milestone video pioneer for IP surveillance", "NECA/IBEW Local 1547 trained craftspeople", "Formal Safety Zone safety program", "One integrated partner for electrical and low-voltage systems"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1971 -> db, /about", "Headquarters Anchorage, Alaska -> db, /", "Employee count 200+ -> db, /about", "Alaskan-owned -> /, /about", "Offices in Anchorage, Fairbanks, Juneau, Wasilla -> /", "Services: commercial electrical, system integration, security, communications, structured cabling, AV, solar, EV charging, NFPA 70B maintenance -> /services", "Industries: healthcare, aviation, corrections, defense, North Slope, industrial -> /, /about", "Project: Providence Alaska Medical Center Tower M -> /", "Project: Eielson AFB F-35 hangars -> /", "Project