UPDATE companies SET description='Alert Tech SMT is an electronics contract manufacturer based in Webster, Texas. The company began as a retail technology business before pivoting to in-house manufacturing to meet demand for scalable, customized production runs. No founding year or ownership details are disclosed.

The firm specializes in turnkey printed circuit board assembly, surface mount technology, full box builds, new product introduction, and prototyping. Its U.S.-based production facility handles PCB fabrication, cable harness assembly, enclosure modification, functional testing, flying-probe inspection, RF performance verification, and repair services including obsolescence management and board refurbishing. The company supports prototype through volume production but does not publish facility size, headcount, or annual volume figures.

Alert Tech serves customers in telecommunications, industrial technology, robotics and drones, military and defense, energy, aerospace, medical devices, and oil and gas. Its client base includes established companies, startups, and federal agencies seeking a single point of contact for sourcing, development, fabrication, and delivery.

The company emphasizes a fully in-house, streamlined process backed by 33-plus years of global sourcing experience, ISO 9001:2015 certification, and IPC-A-610 Class 3 workmanship standards. It differentiates itself through service-driven support, proactive communication, and integrated design-for-manufacturability reviews.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IPC-A-610 Class 3']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["SMT component sourcing and procurement", "PCB fabrication management", "SMT assembly", "Cable harness and point-to-point wiring", "Sub-assembly integration", "Enclosure modification and assembly", "Final unit test (FUT)", "Box build and system integration", "Burn-in testing", "Configure-to-order assembly", "Design for manufacturability (DFM) review", "Prototype and volume production", "New product introduction (NPI) support", "Design review and BOM/configuration control", "Stencil design", "Integrated process development", "Functional testing", "Flying probe testing (TAKAYA)", "Board and system-level testing", "RF performance testing", "Custom test fixture and software development", "Optical inspection", "Compliance testing support", "PCB repair and refurbishment (including FMEA, EOL/obsolescence management)"], "industries": ["Telecommunications", "Industrial Technology", "Robotics and Drones", "Military and Defense", "Energy", "Aerospace", "Medical Devices", "Oil and Gas"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["TAKAYA Flying Probe Tester", "3D printers (for prototyping)", "CO2 laser cutters (for prototyping)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fully in-house turnkey production from procurement through test", "Single point of contact for sourcing, development, fabrication, and delivery", "33+ years of global sourcing experience with established supplier network", "IPC-A-610 Class 3 certified workmanship", "On-site TAKAYA flying probe testing and custom test fixture development"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Webster, Texas -> db", "ISO 9001 certification -> db", "Industries served: Telecommunications, Industrial Technology, Robotics + Drones, Military + Defense, Energy, Aerospace, Medical Devices -> /", "Testimonial mentions Oil + Gas industry -> /", "Company began as retail technology company, pivoted to in-house manufacturing -> /about", "Over 30 years technology development expertise -> /about", "33+ years global sourcing experience -> /capabilities", "Fully in-house turnkey production process -> /", "Single point of contact for sourcing through delivery -> /", "IPC-A-610 Class 3 certified -> / (blog title)", "TAKAYA Flying Probe Tester -> /capabilities", "3D printing and CO2 lasers for prototyping -> /about", "Services: SMT assembly, PCB fabrication, box builds, NPI, prototyping, testing, repair -> /capabilities", "Capabilities include cable harness, sub-assembly, enclosure modification, FUT, burn-in, DFM, design review, stencil design, flying probe, functional test, RF test, optical inspection, compliance test, repair, FMEA, EOL management, board refurbishing -> /capabilities", "Quality management system complies with ISO 9001:2015 -> /about", "No explicit founding year, ownership, founders, employee count, facility size, volume range, lead time, tolerances, CAGE code, min order, export compliance, languages, social links found in INPUT -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Alert Tech SMT is a strategic full stack electronics contract manufacturer specializing in surface mount technology and turnkey printed circuit board assemblies.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='alert-tech-smt' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='All About Packaging Inc. was founded in 1997 in Appleton, Wisconsin, as a family-owned business. The founders set out to resolve a common problem—the requirement of multiple vendors to successfully package a single product—by offering a single source for all packaging needs.

The company manufactures thermoformed packaging, including clamshells, blisters, trays, and custom paper solutions. In-house engineers collaborate on design and engineering, and rapid prototyping capabilities produce working prototypes in five to ten business days. The single-source model also covers fulfillment, distribution, and inventory management.

All About Packaging serves industrial, retail, and medical markets. Its customer base includes Ideal Industries Inc., Innoware Inc., Johnsonville Sausage LLC, and Harley-Davidson Motor Company.

