UPDATE companies SET description='Allied Body Works Inc. has operated from Seattle, Washington since 1949, when Charles Walter Bull and two partners each invested $200 to leave Heiser Body and open a small garage on Fourth Avenue. The company remains family‑owned; after passing through the Bull and Minice lines, Charles’s great‑grandson Adam Keane purchased the business in February 2023 and serves as president.

Today the shop at 625 South 96th Street builds and installs custom truck bodies and upfit solutions for light‑ to medium‑duty vehicles. Services span cargo‑van interiors, service bodies, dump bodies, platform bodies, pickup‑truck accessories, liftgates, cranes, electrical and lighting packages, and the proprietary Walker Blocker side‑guard system. The team of roughly a dozen technicians also handles fabrication, repair, and emerging EV upfit work, serving the greater Pacific Northwest.

Customers include tradespeople, mobile workforces, fleet operators, and government agencies. Early work included armored cars for Loomis; later the company expanded with Seattle’s shipping and distribution sector. Current accounts range from local contractors to municipal fleets needing van upfitting, truck side guards, and turnkey work‑truck packages.

The founders’ original commitment to honest work and fair treatment still drives the culture. Allied emphasizes quick turnaround — meeting deadlines is a stated priority — and the ability to execute complex, one‑off designs. A future‑focused mindset adds safety innovations like the Walker Blocker and green options such as solar‑integrated upfits.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Van upfitting", "Truck upfitting", "Fabrication", "Repair", "EV upfit solutions", "Walker Blocker side guard installation", "Cargo van interior upfitting", "Service body installation", "Dump body installation", "Platform body customization", "Pickup truck accessory installation", "Liftgate installation", "Crane installation", "Electrical and lighting accessory installation", "In-stock ready truck solutions"], "industries": ["Construction", "Utilities", "Delivery and logistics", "Government/fleet", "Mobile workforce", "Shipping and distribution", "Armored car services"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned since 1949, now fourth generation", "Quick installation with deadline-driven scheduling", "Capability to execute complex, custom fabrication from customer plans", "Future-focused safety (Walker Blocker) and green (solar) solutions", "In-stock ready trucks through Work Truck Solutions partnership"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1949 by Charles Walter Bull and two partners with $200 each in a garage on 4th Ave, Seattle -> /about", "Family-owned, passed through generations; Adam Keane (great-grandson) purchased Feb 2023 -> /about", "Address: 625 South 96th St, Seattle, WA 98108 -> /", "Services: van upfitting, truck upfitting, fabrication, repair, EV solutions, Walker Blocker, cargo van interiors, service bodies, dump bodies, platform bodies, pickup truck solutions, liftgates, cranes, electrical/lighting -> /, /services", "Early work: armored cars for Loomis; expanded with Seattle shipping/distribution -> /about", "Customers: tradespeople, mobile workforce, fleet operators, government agencies -> /, /about, /services", "Team list shows ~12 named staff -> /about", "Quick installation, meeting deadlines priority -> /", "Complex solutions capability -> /", "Future-focused: Walker Blocker safety, solar/green -> /", "In-stock ready trucks via Work Truck Solutions partnership -> /", "Company describes itself as full-line Truck Equipment Distributor and Upfitter -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Allied Body Works now handles everything from light duty truck accessories and cargo van interiors, to medium/heavy duty flatbeds, dump bodies, contractor bodies, service bodies, van bodies, cranes, electrical and lighting accessories, liftgates and more.", "founded_year": "1949", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='allied-body-works-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Allied Plastics LLC operates from Twin Lakes, Wisconsin. The company does not publicly disclose its founding year or ownership structure, and no founders are named in available sources.

The company specializes in heavy-gauge vacuum thermoforming and custom sheet extrusion, producing plastic components up to 8 feet by 14 feet by 60 inches thick using material from 0.060 to 0.55 inches. Its capabilities include single-sheet, twin-sheet, drape, pressure, and sheet-over-sheet forming, along with CNC and robotic trimming, die cutting, punching, finishing, hardware installation, bonding, assembly, kitting, inventory management, just-in-time stocking, packaging, labeling, and fulfillment. Allied Plastics runs more than 20 thermoforming machines across a 210,000-square-foot manufacturing facility and a 350,000-square-foot distribution and manufacturing facility.

The company serves agriculture, automotive, medical, construction, lawn and garden, transportation, and industrial markets, as well as packaging and dunnage applications. Customers include OEMs and manufacturers seeking durable parts, reusable packaging, material handling solutions, and custom thermoformed assemblies such as weather-resistant housings, automotive interior and exterior components, medical trays and housings, and industrial enclosures and guards.

Allied Plastics emphasizes an integrated model that combines plastics engineering, manufacturing, finishing, inventory support, and delivery under one roof to reduce handoffs and improve control over quality and lead times. The company cites its senior team’s 30-plus years of thermoforming experience and its in-house extrusion capability as key differentiators for consistent material performance and streamlined production.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 14001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Heavy-gauge vacuum thermoforming", "Single-sheet forming", "Twin-sheet forming", "Drape forming", "Pressure forming", "Sheet-over-sheet forming", "Custom sheet extrusion", "CNC trimming", "Robotic trimming", "Die cutting", "Punching", "Finishing", "Hardware installation", "Bonding", "Assembly", "Kitting", "Inventory management", "Just-in-time (JIT) stocking", "Packaging", "Labeling", "Fulfillment", "Engineering and design support (IDEA Center)", "Prototyping", "Thermoform tooling"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Automotive", "Medical", "Construction", "Lawn and Garden", "Transportation", "Industrial", "Packaging & Dunnage"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["20+ thermoforming machines", "CNC trimming equipment", "Robotic trimming equipment", "Custom sheet extrusion line"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Integrated plastics engineering, manufacturing, finishing, inventory support, and delivery under one roof", "20+ thermoforming machines with part capacity up to 8 ft \u00d7 14 ft \u00d7 60 in", "210,000 sq ft manufacturing facility plus 350,000 sq ft distribution and manufacturing facility", "In-house custom sheet extrusion for greater material control", "Senior team with 30+ years of thermoforming experience"], "facts_used": ["Location: Twin Lakes, Wisconsin -> db", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, ISO 14001:2015 -> /", "Capabilities: heavy-gauge thermoforming, custom sheet extrusion, CNC trimming, finishing, assembly, inventory support -> /", "Facility size: 210,000 sq ft manufacturing, 350,000 sq ft distribution -> /", "Machine count: 20+ thermoforming machines -> /", "Part size: up to 8 ft x 14 ft x 60 in, material thickness .060 to .55 in -> /", "Industries served: agriculture, automotive, medical, construction, lawn and garden, transportation, industrial, packaging & dunnage -> /", "Senior team experience: 30+ years thermoforming experience -> /", "Integrated service model: engineering, manufacturing, finishing, inventory, delivery under one roof -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Allied Plastics provides integrated thermoforming plastic services for manufacturers that need durable parts, reusable packaging, and custom material handling solutions.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/alliedplastics/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='allied-plastics-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Alpha Sheet Metal Works operates from Ladson, South Carolina. The company has served the industrial community for close to 80 years, beginning with custom sheet metal work and the design and fabrication of specialized equipment. Joseph W. Schady serves as president.

The shop works with steel, stainless steel, and aluminum, functioning as both a job shop and a small‑to‑medium‑run contract manufacturer. Its capabilities span laser and waterjet cutting, MIG/TIG/spot welding, sheet metal fabrication, CNC forming on Trumpf and Durma presses, CNC machining, and CAD‑CAM programming. Inspection is handled by a Virtek LaserQC system that captures over 500 data points per second at ±0.002 in tolerance, supplemented by a portable Romer Arm for 3D measurement and reverse engineering.

Alpha serves defense, chemical, automotive, and environmental sectors, as well as broader commercial, industrial, and military markets. Customers range from prototype developers to producers of complete automated assemblies.

