UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Menomonee Falls, Wisconsin, American Cable & Electronics, Inc. (ACE) operates as a manufacturer of custom cable assemblies and electro-mechanical assemblies for original equipment manufacturers. The company focuses on low- to mid-volume production runs and rapid prototyping of complex electromechanical designs.

ACE’s capabilities span engineering, rapid prototyping, and manufacturing of electromechanical assemblies that integrate plastics, sheet metal, electronics, cable assemblies, and plastic injection over-molded parts. The facility handles projects ranging from simple wire harnesses to fully finished assemblies with embedded circuits or over-molded PCBs, and offers turn-key electro-mechanical project management. Services include design for manufacturability, design assistance, material analysis and testing, tooling development, and CAD support.

The company serves medical electronics, industrial controls, commercial products, and defense sectors, including the U.S. and Canadian Departments of Defense. Its customer base includes Tier 1 medical device suppliers and top OEMs in medical, industrial, and commercial markets.

ACE differentiates itself through a global materials procurement strategy aimed at delivering the right components at the right time, a quality system certified to ISO 9001 and compliant with IPC/WHMA-A-620 and UL/CSA standards, and a focus on low-volume over-molding with flexible tooling. The company emphasizes process controls to ensure every product is manufactured correctly the first time.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','IPC/WHMA-A-620','UL/CSA','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Low volume overmolding with flexible tooling", "Custom cable assemblies", "D-sub cable assemblies (all pin configurations)", "BNC RF connector termination for coaxial cable", "High definition video cable assemblies", "Data center cables", "Embedded circuits or overmolded PCB", "Turn-key electro-mechanical projects", "Engineering and rapid prototyping", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Design assistance", "Material analysis and testing", "Tooling development", "CAD services", "Plastic injection over-molding", "Sheet metal fabrication", "Electronic assembly", "Wire harness assembly"], "industries": ["Medical electronics", "Industrial controls", "Commercial products", "Defense (U.S. and Canadian Departments of Defense)", "Medical device manufacturing (Tier 1 supplier)"], "materials": ["Plastics", "Sheet metal", "Electronic components", "Overmolded plastics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low to mid volume manufacturing", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Low-volume overmolding with flexible tooling", "Rapid prototyping for complex electromechanical assemblies", "Global materials procurement strategy", "ISO 9001 certified quality system", "Turn-key electro-mechanical project management"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Menomonee Falls, Wisconsin -> db", "Manufacturer of custom cable assemblies for OEM market -> /", "Specializes in engineering, rapid prototype, and low-volume manufacturing of electromechanical assemblies -> /", "Products range from simple wire assemblies to complex finished assemblies with plastics, sheet metal, electronics, cable assemblies, and over-molded parts -> /", "ISO 9001 registered -> /", "IPC/WHMA-A-620 compliant -> /", "UL/CSA compliant -> /", "RoHS compliant facility -> /", "JCP USA/Canadian Departments of Defense customer -> /", "Tier 1 Medical industry supplier -> /", "Global supplier to Medical, Commercial and Industrial OEMs -> /about-us", "Low to mid volume manufacturing at Menomonee Falls facility -> /about-us", "Engineering services include DFM, design assistance, material analysis/testing, tooling development, CAD services -> /about-us", "Global materials procurement strategy -> /about-us", "Capabilities: low volume overmolding with flexible tooling, custom cable assemblies, D-sub, BNC, HD video, data center cables, embedded circuits/overmolded PCB, turn-key electro-mechanical projects -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Manufacturer of Custom Cables and Cable Assemblies for the OEM Market", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='american-cable-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='American Cable Products LLC was established in November 2002 and is headquartered in Saint Louis, Missouri. The company operates as a minority‑owned business (MBE certified) and provides low‑voltage communication connectivity solutions across all 50 states, Canada, Mexico, and U.S. territories.

The firm delivers end‑to‑end infrastructure services divided into inside‑plant work — structured premise cabling (Cat5e, Cat6, Cat6a, fiber), data‑center design and implementation, hardware configuration, and network infrastructure — and outside‑plant work such as provider connection points, fiber‑optic installations, and campus connectivity. It also integrates security and surveillance systems, including IP camera networks (up to 2,800 cameras on a single project), access control, and biometrics. The company reports nationwide project experience covering more than 500 facilities and 1,000 sites.

Clients span data centers, healthcare, corrections, education, airports, government, retail, and manufacturing. Notable installations include the STL International Airport, a multi‑site healthcare network, a university system, regional retail distribution centers, and an industrial manufacturing complex.

American Cable Products states its mission is to be a one‑stop shop for communication connectivity from provider demarcation to the data center, emphasizing practical, cost‑effective installation and service that exceeds customer expectations. Core values cited are quality, reliability, customer focus, and cost effectiveness.', certifications=ARRAY['MBE Certified (Minority Business Enterprise)','CPUC Certified (California Public Utilities Commission)','St. Louis Lambert International Airport Approved Contractor']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structured premise cabling (Cat5e, Cat6, Cat6a, fiber optic)", "Data center design, build, and implementation", "Hardware configuration and setup", "Network infrastructure installation", "Provider connection point termination", "Fiber optic installation (outside plant)", "Campus connectivity and inter-building connections", "Security camera and video system installation", "Access control and biometric system integration", "System integration (enterprise-wide communication)", "Wireless network deployment (enterprise-grade)", "Voice systems (VoIP and traditional)", "Audio visual conferencing and collaboration systems", "SCADA and industrial IoT connectivity", "Satellite communications (remote/backup)", "Infrastructure consulting", "Ongoing maintenance and support"], "industries": ["Data Centers", "Healthcare", "Corrections", "Education", "Airports", "Government", "Retail", "Manufacturing"], "materials": ["Cat5e", "Cat6", "Cat6a", "Fiber optic"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["MBE certified (Minority Business Enterprise)", "CPUC certified for telecommunications infrastructure", "Approved contractor for St. Louis Lambert International Airport critical infrastructure", "Nationwide service coverage across 50 states, Canada, Mexico, and U.S. territories", "24/7 support availability"], "facts_used": ["Founded November 2002 -> /about", "Headquartered in Saint Louis, Missouri -> /ab