UPDATE companies SET description='American Circuits operates from Charlotte, North Carolina, where it has maintained a family-run, minority-owned electronic contract manufacturing business for more than three decades. The company was founded by Vic Gondha, a first-generation immigrant who built the firm after arriving in the United States with a goal of owning a business that could support his family and community. His son, Ket Gondha, now serves as CEO, having expanded the company''s Charlotte campus after a career on Wall Street.

The firm provides turnkey printed circuit board assembly from two facilities encompassing roughly 40,000 square feet. Its capabilities span PCB fabrication and assembly (surface-mount, through-hole, and mixed technology), rapid prototyping, conformal coating and potting, automated optical inspection, PCB design and reverse engineering, design-for-manufacturability analysis, bill-of-materials optimization, custom wire harness and cable assembly, and full electro-mechanical integration including box builds and subassemblies. Production runs range from single prototypes to volumes exceeding 100,000 units.

The company emphasizes a one-stop model that controls the process from bare-board procurement through final assembly and test.

The founder''s vision centered on offering both bare boards and turnkey assemblies under one roof—a combination he described as rare in the U.S. market. That end-to-end control, coupled with flexible low-to-high volume runs and ITAR-registered, ISO 9001-certified operations, remains the core differentiator the company highlights today.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ITAR registered','UL recognized','RoHS','REACH','Dodd-Frank conflict mineral reporting']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB fabrication", "PCB assembly (SMT, through-hole, mixed technology)", "Turnkey production", "Rapid prototyping", "Conformal coating", "Potting", "Automated optical inspection (AOI)", "PCB design", "Reverse engineering", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Bill of materials (BOM) optimization", "Wire harness assembly", "Cable assembly", "Electro-mechanical assembly", "Box build integration", "Subassembly integration", "Kitting", "Testing", "Supply chain management", "Component sourcing"], "industries": ["Defense", "Healthcare", "Robotics", "LED lighting", "Security and key control systems", "Automotive", "Electronics OEMs"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "1 to 100,000+ units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Controls entire process from bare-board procurement to finished assembly", "Turnkey assembly for prototype quantities from 1 to 100,000+ units", "U.S.-based, ITAR-registered manufacturing with ISO 9001 certification", "Family-run, minority-owned business with over 30 years of operation", "UL recognized, RoHS and REACH compliant"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Charlotte, North Carolina -> db, /", "Founded by Vic Gondha over 30 years ago -> /about-us", "Family-run, minority-owned -> /about-us", "Two facilities totaling ~40,000 sq ft -> /, /about-us", "Services: PCB assembly, turnkey, prototyping, conformal coating, AOI, design, reverse engineering, wire harness, electro-mechanical assembly -> /", "Volume: 1 to 100,000+ units -> /about-u