UPDATE companies SET description='American Control Electronics (ACE), headquartered in South Beloit, Illinois, with a second facility in Chanhassen, Minnesota, has over 60 years of experience in motor control design and manufacturing. The company operates as a subsidiary of Global Point Technologies Group, a motors, gears, and controls conglomerate.

ACE manufactures electronic motor controls, power products, and custom electronic assemblies. Its capabilities span custom circuit design, PCB design and assembly (PCBA), electronic contract manufacturing (EMS), UL508A control panel assembly, wire harness assembly, box build, testing, and long-term manufacturing support. The Chanhassen facility operates under an ISO 9001:2015-certified quality management system, while the South Beloit site supports UL508A panel assembly and in-house UL testing via the UL Data Acceptance Program. The company also offers flexible circuit technologies, sensor integration, wired and wireless interconnectivity, digital graphics, touch screen interfaces, IoT device design, embedded display controllers, switch actuators, and electronic enclosures.

The company serves OEMs across industrial, food processing, medical, home automation, automotive, agriculture, scientific, oil and gas, and sports markets. Its motor control products include DC, AC (VFD), brushless, stepper, and servo drives, as well as gear reducers and accessories.

ACE emphasizes domestic manufacturing flexibility with two U.S. facilities providing production continuity, and a global network of experts across the Americas and Asia to deliver agile manufacturing without heavy capital investment.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','UL508A','UL Data Acceptance Program','UL LISTED','ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Circuit Design", "PCB Design & Assembly (PCBA)", "Electronic Contract Manufacturing (EMS)", "Engineering Design Process", "Testing, Compliance & Support", "UL508A Control Panel Assembly", "Wire Harness Assembly", "Box Build", "Flexible Circuit Technologies (polyester, polyimide, transparent touch sensors, fabric circuits)", "Sensor Integration (multi-sensor, medical, industrial, flexible force, non-invasive fluid level)", "Wired and Wireless Interconnectivity Support", "Digital Graphics (dead-fronted, offset/screen/digital printing, thermoformed designs)", "Touch Screen Interface (capacitive, infrared, membrane, 3D gesturing)", "Internet of Things (IoT) Device Design and Manufacturing", "Embedded Display Controllers", "Switch Actuators (tactile, non-tactile, 3D gesturing)", "Enclosures for Electronics (mechatronics, in-mold decorating, in-mold electronics)", "Custom Motor Controls", "DC Motor Controls", "AC Motor Controls (VFDs)", "Brushless Motor Controls", "Stepper Motor Controls", "Servo Motor Controls", "Gear Reducers"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Food Processing", "Medical", "Home Automation", "Automotive", "Agriculture", "Scientific", "Oil & Gas", "Sports"], "materials": ["Polyester", "Polyimide"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015-certified quality management system at Chanhassen facility", "UL508A panel assembly and in-house UL testing via UL Data Acceptance Program at South Beloit facility", "Domestic manufacturing flexibility with two U.S. facilities ensuring production continuity", "Global network of experts across the Americas and Asia for agile manufacturing", "Full-service custom electronics from circuit design through PCB assembly, wire harness, box build, and long-term support"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in South Beloit, Illinois and Chanhassen, Minnesota -> /", "Over 60 years experience in motor control design and manufacturing -> /", "Subsidiary of Global Point Technologies Group -> /", "Manufactures electronic motor controls, power products, custom electronic assemblies -> /", "Capabilities: custom circuit design, PCB design & assembly, EMS, UL508A panel assembly, wire harness, box build, testing -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 at Chanhassen facility -> /", "UL508A panel assembly and UL Data Acceptance Program at South Beloit -> /", "Industries served: Industrial, Food Processing, Medical, Home, Automotive, Agriculture, Scientific, Oil & Gas, Sports -> /", "Flexible circuit technologies: polyester and polyimide circuits -> /capabilities", "Sensor integration, interconnectivity, digital graphics, touch screen, IoT, embedded display controllers, switch actuators, enclosures -> /capabilities", "Motor control products: DC, AC VFD, brushless, stepper, servo, gear reducers -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "manufactures electronic motor controls, power products, and custom electronic assemblies for industrial, commercial, vehicle, medical, and home automation markets", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='american-control-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='American Electric Components, Inc. has operated from Vernon, California since its founding in 1995. The company is family-owned and operated, drawing on over a century of cumulative experience across its team to design, fabricate, and repair transformers.

The 78,400-square-foot property houses a 47,000-square-foot shop where the company manufactures and repairs single- and three-phase transformers, both dry and oil-filled, with ratings up to 10,000 KVA and 69,000 volts. All units are engineered to meet or exceed NEMA, ANSI, IEEE, and UL standards. The facility also maintains a large inventory of new, rebuilt, and repaired transformers available for immediate sale or rental.

AEC serves utility, industrial, and commercial customers nationwide, including desalination plants requiring desalter transformer overhauls. It holds certified repair-center status from ABB and General Electric, with factory-trained technicians performing service work to original manufacturer standards.

