UPDATE companies SET description='American Howa Kentucky, Inc. Georgetown Plant (AHK‑GT) was established in 2017 in Midway, Kentucky, as the fourth U.S. production site for HOWA USA Holdings, Inc. The Japanese parent, HOWA, operates 33 manufacturing and R&D facilities across over a dozen countries. The Kentucky operation began in 2007 with a plant in Bowling Green, adding sunshade and dash insulator production the following year.

The plant is part of a North American network that includes facilities in Bowling Green, Delaware (Ohio), Canton (Mississippi), and Alliston (Ontario).

The plant serves automotive original equipment manufacturers and Tier 1 suppliers. Key customers include Nissan North America, Toyota Motor North America, American Honda Motor Co., Aisin World Corp. of America, and Webasto Product North America. Programs supported range from the Nissan Leaf and Frontier to the Murano and Titan, as well as Honda headliner programs.

