UPDATE companies SET description='American Wood Design, Inc. is a family-owned commercial cabinetry and architectural millwork shop based in Chester, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1996 by Michael Gilhool Sr., the business began after his position at a Philadelphia paint company’s display shop was eliminated; he bartered the shop’s machinery for his first two store-fixture jobs and started production above a doctor’s office in South Philadelphia. After nearly two decades at Naamans Road Business Park, the company relocated to Chester in 2017, expanding from 5,000 to 16,000 square feet.

The shop produces custom cabinets, countertops, reception desks, nurse stations, office front systems, wall paneling, trim, mouldings, and wood base. It runs plastic laminate layups, solid-surface fabrication, and granite, marble, and quartz countertop work. Core processes include CNC routing, computerized beam saw cutting, and edgebanding, supported by software that drives the machinery. The 16,000-square-foot facility is set up for high-volume production runs while remaining nimble enough for small projects.

Early work included a reception desk for M.A.B. Paints; today the firm serves office fit-outs, medical facilities needing custom nurse stations, and retail chains requiring store fixtures and wall systems.

The company emphasizes building cabinetry and relationships that last a lifetime, delivering craftsmanship on time and on budget. It differentiates itself with fast lead times — offering 3- to 5-day turnaround on wholesale plastic laminate panel layups — and a willingness to handle both large production runs and one-off jobs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Commercial cabinetry", "Architectural millwork", "Custom countertops (plastic laminate, solid surface, granite, marble, quartz)", "Reception desks", "Nurse stations", "Office front systems", "Wall paneling", "Custom trims and mouldings", "Wood base", "Priming and finishing", "Plastic laminate layups (wholesale)", "Plastic laminate repairs", "Modification work", "Maintenance and service calls", "CNC routing", "Beam saw cutting", "Edgebanding"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Healthcare", "Retail", "Architectural millwork", "Office furniture and fit-outs"], "materials": ["Plastic laminate", "Solid surface", "Granite", "Marble", "Quartz", "Wood"], "equipment": ["Computerized beam saw", "CNC router", "Edgebander", "Software to drive machinery"], "volume": "High production runs and small projects", "lead_time": "3-5 days for plastic laminate layups; quick turnover projects", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1996", "16,000 sq ft facility with CNC router, beam saw, and edgebander", "3-5 day turnaround on wholesale plastic laminate layups", "Capable of high-volume production runs and small custom jobs", "Wholesale dealer for plastic laminate panel layups"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 -> db", "Family-owned -> /, /about", "Headquarters Chester, PA -> /, /about", "Founder Michael Gilhool Sr. -> /about", "Started above doctor''s office in South Philadelphia -> /about", "Moved to Naamans Road Business Park for nearly 20 years -> /about", "Moved to Chester, PA in 2017, expanding from 5,000 to 16,000 sq ft -> /about", "Equipment: computerized beam saw, CNC router, edgebander -> /about", "Services: plastic laminate layups, cabinets, countertops, reception desks, nurse stations, architectural millwork, custom millwork, solid surface fabrication, repairs -> /services", "Plastic laminate layups wholesale, 3-5 day turnaround -> /services", "Custom millwork: 100LF minimum orders -> /services", "Mission: build cabinetry and relationships that last a lifetime -> /", "Fast lead times, quick turnover projects -> /", "Serving Greater Philadelphia region -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "American Wood Design, Inc. is a family owned and operated commercial cabinetry business", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "100 linear feet for custom millwork (trims/mouldings)", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='american-wood-design-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Americor Electronics Ltd. was founded in 1988 by Tom Pross in Elk Grove Village, Illinois. Pross brought 22 years of experience in power cord, cable, and wire harness production to the venture, establishing a supplier network that spans the globe.

The company manufactures custom and standard power cords (including locking, medical, and international configurations), cable assemblies, and wire harnesses. It also produces a range of electronic components such as solenoids, relays, axial fans, terminal blocks, piezo electric devices, EMI/RFI filters, and transformers. Beyond fabrication, Americor provides prototyping, testing support, documentation for approval, and post-order inventory management with scheduled shipping. Standard items are sourced from overseas partners, while custom designs are built to customer specifications.

Americor serves original equipment manufacturers and distributors exclusively, with a focus on the appliance, electric, and electronic industries. Longtime customers include Pulsafeeder, an Idex Corporation business that named Americor its 2019 Supplier of the Year. The firm also acts as the U.S. manufacturer''s representative for Germany''s Adels Contact, supplying terminal blocks, connector systems, and high-power LED distribution boxes.

Pross founded the business to leverage his deep supplier relationships and deliver custom products that guarantee maximum function and cost efficiency. The operation maintains ISO 9001:2015 certification and RoHS compliance, and holds membership in the Wiring Harness Manufacturer''s Association.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable assembly and wire harness manufacturing", "Power cord manufacturing (standard, locking, medical, international)", "Custom electronic component manufacturing", "Prototyping and testing support", "Inventory management and scheduled shipping", "Documentation for submittal and approval", "Overseas sourcing for standard components", "Manufacturer''s representation for Adels Contact terminal blocks and connector systems", "ISO 9001:2015 quality management", "RoHS compliance"], "industries": ["Original Equipment Manufacturers (OEM)", "Appliance manufacturing", "Electric and electronic components", "Medical devices (power cords)", "Industrial equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 certified and RoHS compliant", "Custom products designed to customer specifications with prototyping and testing support", "Inventory management and scheduled shipping after order", "U.S. representative for Adels Contact terminal blocks and connector systems", "Wiring Harness Manufacturer''s Association member"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1988 by Tom Pross -> /about", "Headquarters in Elk Grove Village, Illinois -> /about, db", "ISO 9001:2015 certified and RoHS compliant -> /, /about", "Manufactures power cords, cable assemblies, wire harnesses, electronic components -> /, /about", "Provides prototyping, testing, documentation, inventory management -> /, /about", "Serves OEMs and distributors exclusively -> /, /about", "Customer Pulsafeeder (Idex Corporation) awarded Supplier of the Year 2019 -> /", "U.S. manufacturer''s representative for Adels Contact (Germany) -> /", "Wiring Harness Manufacturer''s Association member -> /", "Tom Pross had 22 years experience prior to founding -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Manufacturing power cords, cable & wire harnesses and other electric and electronic components for the world since 1988.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='americor-electronics-ltd' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ameriprint Apparel has operated from Sun Prairie, Wisconsin since 1985. The shop serves the Madison metro area and runs Monday through Friday, 9 a.m. to 5 p.m.

The company provides custom decoration services including screen printing for vibrant, durable bulk orders; embroidery for uniforms and promotional items; direct-to-film (DTF) and digital printing for full-color, on-demand designs on cotton and cotton-blend fabrics; and laser engraving on drinkware, awards, leather, and acrylic. It also sources promotional products such as tote bags, drinkware, pens, and headwear, and offers inventory storage and fulfillment for client webstores. All production occurs in-house at the Sun Prairie facility.

Recent orders highlighted in reviews include team apparel for a Lithuanian dance festival, shirts for an American Legion post, fraternity t-shirts, and family reunion tops. The business also handles trade-show giveaways, employee onboarding kits, and holiday corporate gifts.

Ameriprint emphasizes its in-house graphics team and an online design tool that lets customers create or refine artwork. The company also promotes inventory storage and fulfillment as a way to streamline recurring orders, and notes that it can accommodate small orders alongside large runs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Screen printing", "Embroidery", "DTF printing", "Digital printing", "Laser engraving", "Promotional product sourcing", "Inventory storage and fulfillment", "Custom webstore setup", "Logo cleanup", "Holiday corporate gifts", "Trade show and event giveaways", "Employee appreciation kits", "Laser name badges", "Engraved gifts"], "industries": ["Schools", "Sports teams", "Corporate", "Events and trade shows", "Employee recognition"], "materials": ["Cotton", "Cotton-blend fabrics", "Drinkware", "Awards", "Leather", "Acrylic"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house graphics team and online design tool", "Inventory storage and fulfillment for client webstores", "DTF and digital printing for on-demand full-color designs", "Laser engraving on drinkware, awards, leather, and acrylic", "Screen printing and embroidery produced in-house at Sun Prairie shop"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1985 -> /about-us", "Located at 1708 Sunfield Street, Sun Prairie, WI -> /about-us", "Offers screen printing, embroidery, DTF/digital printing, laser engraving, promotional products -> /", "Provides inventory storage and fulfillment -> /", "Serves schools, teams, corporate, events, trade shows, employee gifts -> /", "In-house graphics team and online designer -> /about-us", "Customer reviews mention quick turnaround and design assistance -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a custom screen-printing and embroidery company located in Sun Prairie, Wisconsin", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ameriprint-apparel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Amphenol DC Electronics, based in San Jose, California, was founded in 1979 by David Cianciulli after he left Hughes Aircraft. The company was acquired by Amphenol in 2013 and operates as a division of that global interconnect manufacturer.

The company designs, engineers, and manufactures custom wire harnesses, cable assemblies, and integrated electronic mechanical devices (box builds). Its services include overmolded cable assemblies, discrete assemblies, and value‑added services such as in‑house tooling, lean manufacturing, and engineering liaison. Production takes place in a 70,000‑square‑foot facility in Silicon Valley, with additional manufacturing sites in Nogales, Mexico, and Malaysia.

Amphenol DC Electronics serves medical device manufacturers (MRI, CT, X‑ray, patient monitoring, surgical robotics), aerospace and military customers (including Trimble for handheld GPS during the Gulf War), defense contractors, industrial equipment makers (factory automation robotics), and precision agriculture equipment producers. The company holds ISO 13485:2016 for medical, ITAR registration, and IPC‑620 Class III certification for electronic assemblies.

The company emphasizes its singular focus on custom cable and wire harness assemblies for over 30 years, which it says provides deep expertise to identify design and manufacturability issues early. It highlights continual improvement, lean practices across information and material flow, in‑house engineering and design liaison for build‑to‑print proficiency, and personalized customer support with prompt order fulfillment.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','ITAR','IPC-620:2016 Class III','UL 508','UL 764','C-TPAT','GDEP','SAM']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable harnesses & assemblies", "Integrated electronic mechanical devices (box builds)", "Overmolded cable assemblies", "Discrete assemblies", "Medical device cable assemblies", "In\u2011house engineering & design liaison", "Lean manufacturing", "In\u2011house tooling & prototyping", "CNC machining (30/55/85 ton presses)", "Clean room assembly (Class 1000, 10000)", "Cable braiding", "Ruggedized assemblies", "Fiber optic cable assemblies", "Smart cable assembly", "Semi\u2011rigid coax cable", "Sub\u2011miniature coax cabling", "Custom CAT5/6 cable assemblies", "UL certified assemblies", "IPC\u2011620 Class III certified parts", "Build\u2011to\u2011print", "Design for manufacturability", "Quick\u2011turn prototyping"], "industries": ["Medical Device", "Aerospace & Defense", "RF Coaxial", "Industrial Equipment", "Agriculture"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CNC machine shop with 30 ton, 55 ton, and 85 ton presses", "Class 1000 clean work area", "Class 10,000 clean work area"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single focus on custom cable and wire harness assemblies for over 30 years", "In\u2011house engineering and design liaison for build\u2011to\u2011print proficiency", "Lean manufacturing applied to production floor and information/material flow", "ITAR registered and ISO 13485:2016 certified"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1979 by David Cianciulli -> /about", "Acquired by Amphenol in 2013 -> /", "70,000 sq ft facility in San Jose -> db", "Additional sites in Nogales, Mexico and Malaysia -> /about", "Custom cable harnesses, wire harnesses, box builds -> /", "Overmolded cable assemblies -> /", "Discrete assemblies -> /", "Medical device cables (MRI, patient monitoring, surgical robotics) -> /", "ISO 13485:2016 certification -> /", "ITAR registration -> /", "IPC-620:2016 Class III certification -> /", "UL 508, UL 764 certifications -> /", "C-TPAT, GDEP, SAM registrations -> /", "CNC machine shop with 30/55/85 ton presses -> /", "Class 1000 and 10,000 clean work areas -> /", "Industries: Medical, Aerospace/Military, Industrial, Agriculture -> /", "Trimble GPS cable ramp-up during Gulf War -> /about", "Lean manufacturing and continual improvement -> /", "In-house engineering/design liaison -> /", "Single focus on custom cable/wire harness for 30+ years -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Amphenol DC Electronics is a custom cable assembly and wire harness manufacturing company. We specialized in the design, engineering, and manufacturing of custom wire harnesses, cable assemblies, and integrated electronic mechanical devices (box builds).", "founded_year": "1979", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered", "SAM", "GDEP", "C-TPAT"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='amphenol-dc-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Amphenol TPC Wire & Cable is headquartered in Macedonia, Ohio. The company traces its origins to 1979 when it began supplying high-performance wire and cable engineered for harsh industrial environments. No founders are named in public sources, and the ownership structure beyond the Amphenol branding is not detailed.

The company manufactures and supplies a range of products including wire, cable, connectors, cable assemblies, cable management systems, cordsets, and electrical components. It also offers custom-engineered solutions designed by an in-house team of electrical, industrial, and mechanical engineers. No facility size, headcount, or production volumes are publicly disclosed.

Amphenol TPC serves a broad set of industries: automotive, food and beverage, general manufacturing, industrial automation, metals, mining, oil and gas, rail and transit, shipyard and marine, utility and power transmission, and wood, pulp, and paper. Customer testimonials cite applications in welding operations, freezer environments, and shipyard welding cable installations.

The company emphasizes its role as a problem-solver, providing abuse-resistant cables that withstand abrasion, chemicals, extreme temperatures, flexing, impact, and tension. A noted case study reports a shipyard saving $286,000 over two years by switching to the company''s Super-Trex® 600 Volt Welding Cable.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable assembly", "Cable assembly manufacturing", "Wire and cable manufacturing", "Connector assembly", "Cable management systems", "Cordset manufacturing", "Custom engineering and design", "Harsh environment cable solutions"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Food and Beverage", "General Manufacturing", "Industrial Automation", "Metals", "Mining", "Oil and Gas", "Rail & Transit", "Ship Yard / Marine", "Utility and Power Transmission", "Wood, Pulp, and Paper"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom-engineered cable and connector solutions tailored to specific applications", "Products engineered to withstand abrasion, chemicals, cold, flexing, high heat, impact, and tension", "In-house electrical, industrial, and mechanical engineering team for custom designs", "Documented reduction in downtime and maintenance costs (e.g., shipyard saved $286,000 in two years)"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Macedonia, Ohio -> db", "Founded 1979 (since 1979) -> /about-us", "Product lines: wire, cable, connectors, assemblies, cable management, cordsets, electrical components, custom solutions -> /about-us", "Industries served list -> /about-us", "Custom engineering team (electrical, industrial, mechanical) -> /about-us", "Mission and values (agility, trust, performance, collaboration) -> /about-us", "Case study: shipyard saved $286,000 with Super-Trex welding cable -> /about-us", "Testimonials referencing welding, freezer, chemical environments -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Amphenol TPC Wire & Cable is a leading supplier of high-performance wire, cable, connectors, and assemblies designed and engineered to withstand harsh industrial environments.", "founded_year": "1979", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='amphenol-tpc-wire-cable' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ampleon USA Inc. maintains a sales and engineering office in Smithfield, Rhode Island, as part of the global Ampleon organization headquartered in Nijmegen, Netherlands. The company operates a dedicated production facility in Cabuyao, Philippines, and holds additional sales offices across China, Finland, France, Korea, Sweden, Taiwan, and a second U.S. location in Dallas, Texas.

The company designs and manufactures RF power transistors, including gallium-nitride-on-silicon-carbide (GaN-on-SiC) HEMT devices and silicon LDMOS discrete transistors. These components serve 5G New Radio infrastructure such as massive MIMO arrays with up to 128 simultaneous streams, high-efficiency small cells, and high-power macro base stations. Ampleon also supplies solid-state RF generators for particle accelerators and industrial heating applications, with power levels ranging from kilowatts to megawatts.

Ampleon’s customer base spans telecommunications equipment makers, industrial and scientific research facilities, and medical technology manufacturers. The company’s distribution network covers the Americas, EMEA, South Asia Pacific, Japan, China, and Korea, supported by a team of manufacturer’s representatives covering all 50 U.S. states and international distributors.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["GaN-on-SiC HEMT transistor design and fabrication", "Silicon LDMOS discrete transistor manufacturing", "5G base station RF power amplifier solutions (mMIMO, small cell, macro)", "Particle accelerator RF power systems", "Industrial heating RF generator design", "Global sales, application engineering, and distribution support"], "industries": ["Telecommunications", "Industrial", "Scientific", "Medical", "Particle Accelerator", "Industrial Heating"], "materials": ["GaN on SiC", "Silicon (LDMOS)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Market-leading RF power solutions for 5G mMIMO up to 128 simultaneous streams", "High-efficiency small cell and high-power macro base station transistors", "Solid-state GaN-on-SiC HEMTs for particle accelerators and industrial heating (kW to MW)", "Global production site in the Philippines with worldwide sales and distribution network", "ITAR-registered for defense and aerospace applications"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Nijmegen, Netherlands; US office in Smithfield, RI; production site in Cabuyao, Philippines -> /", "RF power solutions for 5G mMIMO, small cell, macro base stations -> description", "GaN-on-SiC HEMT transistors for particle accelerators and industrial heating -> description", "LDMOS discrete transistors -> description", "ITAR certification -> certifications", "Industries: Industrial, Scientific and Medical -> industries_served", "Global sales representatives covering all 50 US states -> /", "Distribution partners across Americas, EMEA, APAC, Japan, China, Korea -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Ampleon Production Site in Cabuyao, Philippines; providing market leading RF power solutions for mMIMO", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ampleon-usa-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Amsted Automotive, headquartered in Saginaw, Michigan, was formed in 2021 through the integration of Burgess-Norton (established 1903) and Means Industries (established 1922), along with Transform Automotive (1997) and SMW Manufacturing (2004). The combined entity operates 21 facilities across North America, Europe, and Asia.

The company designs and manufactures high-performance components for vehicle and industrial applications, including brackets, welded assemblies, coupler components, piston pins, bearing products, wear parts, and powertrain components. Core processes include cold forming, powder metallurgy, advanced metal forming (flow forming, in-die spline forming, grob forming, laser welding, stamping), and propulsion systems (torque management, clutch technologies). With over 2,000 employees across 21 facilities worldwide (13 in the U.S.), Amsted produces more than 200 million components annually.

Amsted serves global automotive, off-highway, mining, and industrial markets. Its components are used in electric heavy-duty e-axles, wheel-end bolts and hubs, traditional and hybrid powertrains, brake systems, electric drivelines, chassis and suspension systems, fluid conveyance, and industrial cutting tools.

The company emphasizes its regional manufacturing footprint—13 U.S. facilities plus global sites—to mitigate tariff risks and supply delays, enabling production close to customer demand. Its integration of legacy brands brings together cold forming, powder metallurgy, and advanced metal forming expertise to deliver tailored, high-quality components for evolving propulsion technologies.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cold forming", "Powder metallurgy", "Advanced metal forming (flow forming, in-die spline forming, grob forming, laser welding, stamping)", "Propulsion systems (torque management, clutch technologies)", "Complex assemblies", "Net-shape manufacturing", "Value engineering", "High-density powder metal parts", "Intricate geometry manufacturing"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Off-highway", "Mining", "Industrial", "Electric vehicle", "Hybrid vehicle", "Internal combustion engine", "Transportation"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Over 200 million components annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Regional manufacturing footprint with 13 U.S. facilities to minimize tariff risks and supply delays", "Over 200 million components produced annually across 21 global facilities", "Integrated cold forming, powder metallurgy, and advanced metal forming capabilities under one organization", "Propulsion solutions covering electrified, hybrid, and internal combustion powertrain architectures", "Net-shape cold forming with uninterrupted grain flow for superior strength and reliability"], "facts_used": ["HQ Saginaw, Michigan -> db", "Founded 1903 (Burgess-Norton) -> db", "Employee count 2000 -> db", "Formed in 2021 via integration of Burgess-Norton (1903) and Means Industries (1922) -> /about", "Over 200 million components annually -> / and /about", "11 US manufacturing facilities listed -> / and /about", "Capabilities: cold forming, powder metallurgy, advanced metal forming, propulsion systems -> /capabilities