UPDATE companies SET description='Anderson Electric Co. was founded in 2020 in Aberdeen, South Dakota, by Shaine Anderson. A family‑owned electrical contracting firm, it traces its roots to Anderson’s start in the trade at the end of 2005. He spent nearly six years with a local contractor learning residential, commercial, and street‑lighting work, then helped construct the Aberdeen beef plant where he gained experience with 480 V switchgear and low‑voltage control systems. After the plant closed, he returned to construction and service work before joining the new plant owners to oversee electrical and fabrication‑floor maintenance departments for more than five years. Seeing a need for healthier client relationships and stronger workplace leadership, Anderson launched his own company built on the values of integrity, quality, and service.

The company designs, installs, repairs, and maintains electrical systems across residential, commercial, farm, and industrial sectors. Specialized services include industrial electrical maintenance, industrial project design, controls and automation, custom lighting projects, and smart‑home technology integration. All installed equipment is UL listed, and the firm is licensed, insured, and bonded in South Dakota with reciprocity in other states.

Anderson Electric serves homeowners, businesses, agricultural operations, and industrial facilities in and around Aberdeen. Recent projects cited by customers include converting a 1950s church into a café with modern lighting and kitchen outlets, installing bathroom‑fan ducting and wiring, updating wiring in older homes, and providing industrial maintenance for a beef‑processing plant. The firm also works with general contractors on new construction and renovation projects.

The company says its differentiation lies in its core values—integrity (no cutting corners, UL‑listed equipment), quality (exceeding code requirements), and service (vetted employees, “extra mile” attitude). Anderson also emphasizes a purpose‑driven model: each month the business donates to organizations such as Destiny Rescue, Coffee with a Cause, and Aberdeen’s Safe Harbor, linking its commercial work to community impact.', certifications=ARRAY['UL Listed']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical system design", "Electrical installation", "Electrical repair", "Electrical maintenance", "Industrial electrical maintenance", "Industrial electrical project design", "Controls and automation", "Custom lighting design and installation", "Smart home technology integration", "Residential electrical wiring", "Commercial electrical wiring", "Farm electrical systems", "Street lighting installation and maintenance", "Low-voltage control systems", "480V switchgear systems"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Farm", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated", "UL-listed equipment installed on every job", "Licensed, insured, and bonded in South Dakota", "Specializes in industrial electrical maintenance and controls/automation", "Employees vetted for safety and privacy"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2020 -> /about-us", "Family-owned -> /about-us and /", "Headquarters in Aberdeen, South Dakota -> /", "Owner Shaine Anderson -> / and /about-us", "Shaine Anderson background (2005 start, local contractor, beef plant construction, maintenance oversight) -> /about-us", "Services: residential, commercial, farm, industrial electrical -> /", "Specializations: industrial electrical maintenance, project design, controls and automation, custom lighting, smart home -> /", "UL listed equipment installed -> /", "Licensed, insured, bonded in South Dakota -> /about-us", "Core values: Integrity, Quality, Service -> /", "Monthly charitable donations to Destiny Rescue, Coffee with a Cause, Safe Harbor -> / and /about-us", "Customer project examples (church to cafe, bathroom fan, old house wiring, beef plant maintenance) -> /", "UL Listed certification -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Anderson Electric is a family-owned electrical contracting business, serving the needs of Aberdeen, SD and the surrounding area.", "founded_year": "2020", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='anderson-electric-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Andon Electronics Corporation is based in Lincoln, Rhode Island. The company is led by John O. Tate, who serves as president and is credited as the developer of the precision semiconductor socket contact. No founding year or ownership details are provided.

Andon manufactures innovative precision sockets used to place image sensors, optoelectronic sensors, gas sensors, DC-DC converters, batteries, crystal oscillators, fuses, relays, and other electronic devices onto printed circuit boards. The product line includes sockets categorized by device type—such as image sensor, optoelectronic sensor, gas sensor, power converter, crystal oscillator, battery, fuse, and display—and by package type, including PGA, BGA, LCC, DIP (closed and open frame), SIP, transistor outline (TO), PLCC, and LED. Specialty offerings encompass Heat Sink Sockets™, high-temperature sockets, terminals, test jacks, ultra-low profile sockets, floating pin sockets, and laminate wafer sockets without circuitry. The company provides both standard and custom socket solutions.

Andon’s sockets are used by original equipment manufacturers (OEMs) and contract manufacturers (CMs) across sectors such as camera production, laser manufacturing, and gas sensing equipment. OEMs and CMs adopt Andon sockets to avoid device damage, reduce board assembly labor, and improve turnaround times.

The company emphasizes its innovative socket designs for optimum device protection, a capability rooted in Tate’s development of the precision semiconductor socket contact. This focus on protecting sensitive components during assembly and streamlining the manufacturing process is presented as its core differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision semiconductor socket manufacturing", "Custom socket design", "Standard socket production", "High-temperature socket manufacturing", "Ultra-low profile socket manufacturing", "Floating pin socket manufacturing", "Laminate wafer socket manufacturing (no circuitry)", "Heat sink socket manufacturing", "Terminal and test jack manufacturing", "Image sensor socket placement", "Optoelectronic sensor socket placement", "Gas sensor socket placement", "DC-DC converter socket placement", "Battery socket placement", "Crystal oscillator socket placement", "Fuse socket placement", "Relay socket placement"], "industries": ["OEMs", "Contract manufacturers", "Camera manufacturing", "Laser manufacturing", "Gas sensing equipment manufacturing", "Chungwa Telecom Labs", "Micropac Industries"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Lincoln, Rhode Island -> db", "John O. Tate is president and developer of precision semiconductor socket contact -> page /", "Company makes innovative precision sockets for placement of various electronic devices onto PC boards -> page /", "Socket product lines by device type and package type listed -> page /", "Specialty sockets: Heat Sink Sockets, Hi-Temp Sockets, Ultra-Low Profile, Floating Pin, Laminate Wafer -> page /", "Customers include OEMs and CMs, specifically Chungwa Telecom Labs and Micropac Industries -> db and page /", "Leading makers of cameras, lasers, gas sensing equipment use Andon sockets -> db", "ISO 9001 certification -> db and page /", "Differentiators: avoid device damage, reduce assembly labor, improve turnaround -> page /", "No founding year, employee count, ownership details provided -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Andon Electronics makes innovative precision sockets used in the placement of image sensors, optoelectronic and gas sensors, DC-DC converters, batteries, crystal oscillators, fuses, relays, and other electronic devices onto PC boards.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='andon-electronics-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Andrew Technologies, Inc. operates as an electronic contract manufacturer from its facility in Wheeling, Illinois. The company specializes in printed circuit board assembly services for businesses across the United States, taking customer designs, fabrication data, and parts lists to produce finished board assemblies.

The shop provides a range of PCB assembly processes including surface-mount technology (SMT), pin-through-hole assembly, and press-fit component insertion. Value-added services encompass device programming, functional testing, rework, cable installation, special packaging, and parts procurement to fulfill customer bill-of-materials requirements.

Andrew Technologies serves technology and production companies nationwide that require outsourced circuit board assembly. The company explicitly notes that it does not repair consumer electronics, appliances, or industrial equipment, focusing exclusively on new assembly work.

